.TH BOOT-REPAIR-LEGACY 1 "2026-09-21" "Boot Bitch 0.2.25" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boot-repair-legacy \- legacy Boot Bitch recovery launcher and console menu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boot-repair-legacy
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIhelper-command\fR [\fIargs\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boot-repair-legacy
is the legacy launcher for the ported
.B boot-repair-legacy-helper
on Debian 4.0
.RI ( "etch" )
and KDE 3.5-era systems. With no arguments it opens a dialog/console menu for
the documented read-only and safe-repair commands; with a helper command it
elevates and runs that command directly. The helper keeps all of its own
runtime preflights and the modern
.B "Repair tool"
/
.B "Repair change status"
evidence contract; this launcher only selects commands and elevates.
.PP
Elevation uses
.BR gksu " --sudo-mode, " gksudo ,
.BR sudo ,
or a plain
.B su
TTY prompt, in that order; no passphrase is ever placed on the command line.
The helper is resolved from
.BR --helper ,
then the
.B BOOT_REPAIR_LEGACY_HELPER
environment variable, then the installed path
.IR /usr/sbin/boot-repair-legacy-helper .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the launcher version.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list\-commands
List the documented helper commands.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tui
Force the console/dialog menu.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-helper
Print the resolved helper path and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-helper " PATH"
Use PATH as the helper.
.TP
.BI \-\-terminal " PATH"
Terminal emulator used by the desktop launch path.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-elevate
Run without elevation (the caller must already be root).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the helper command that would run, then exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate <disk> <root>
Confirm the selected root is a supported target.
.TP
.B diagnose <disk> <root> all
Read-only diagnostics and capability probes.
.TP
.B fs-inspect <disk> <root>
Read-only filesystem inspection.
.TP
.B repair <disk> <root> fix-broken
Safe repair: restore broken package state.
.TP
.B repair <disk> <root> dpkg-configure
Safe repair: finish pending dpkg configuration.
.TP
.B repair <disk> <root> initramfs
Safe repair: rebuild the target initramfs.
.TP
.B repair <disk> <root> apt-update
Safe repair: refresh package metadata (mirror-gated).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/boot-repair-legacy
This launcher.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/boot-repair-legacy-helper
The ported privileged helper.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/boot-repair-legacy.desktop
Desktop entry.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dialog (1),
.BR gksu (1),
.BR sudo (8)
